# Home Assistant glossary

This page covers every entry in the [official Home Assistant glossary](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/glossary/), checked on 12 November 2026. The explanations are civica’s own words, not a copy of the official ones.

Read [Home Assistant terminology](home-assistant-terminology.html) before you use an explanation as a label. For states, device classes and platform names, see [Entity and state language](entity-and-state-language.html).

## Terms that are easy to mix up

An integration supplies entities. A device can group several of them. A trigger starts an automation, a condition checks whether it carries on, and an action asks for something to happen. Saving an automation does not mean it ran. Sending a notification does not mean anyone read it.

