## Browse the glossary

<% register = JSON.parse(File.read(File.join(root, 'data', 'ha-terminology.json'))) %>
<% sources = register['sources'].to_h { |source| [source['id'], source] } %>
<% entries = register['terms'].select { |term| term['category'] == 'official-glossary' }.sort_by { |term| term['native_name'].downcase } %>
<% letters = entries.map { |term| term['native_name'][0].upcase }.uniq %>
<nav aria-label="Glossary letters"><p><% letters.each_with_index do |letter, index| %><%= ' · ' unless index.zero? %><a href="#letter-<%= letter.downcase %>"><%= letter %></a><% end %></p></nav>

<% letters.each do |letter| %>
<h2 id="letter-<%= letter.downcase %>"><%= letter %></h2>
<% entries.select { |term| term['native_name'][0].upcase == letter }.each do |term| %>
<details class="civica-audit-detail" id="<%= escape(term['id'].downcase) %>">
<summary><strong><%= escape(term['native_name']) %></strong><%= ' — historical term retained' if term['status'] == 'historical-term-retained' %></summary>
<p><strong>Say:</strong> <%= escape(term['household_wording']) %>.</p>
<p><strong>What it means:</strong> <%= escape(term['first_use_explanation']) %></p>
<p><strong>Do not confuse it with:</strong> <%= escape(term['avoid_confusion']) %></p>
<% unless term['aliases'].empty? %><p><strong>Also called:</strong> <%= escape(term['aliases'].join(', ')) %>.</p><% end %>
<p><a href="<%= escape(term['official_glossary_url']) %>">Official <%= escape(term['native_name']) %> entry</a><% if term['further_reading_url'] %> · <a href="<%= escape(term['further_reading_url']) %>">Related official guidance</a><% end %>. Reference: <code><%= escape(term['id']) %></code>.</p>
</details>
<% end %>
<% end %>

## Old names

- Apps used to be called add-ons.
- Lovelace still appears in technical dashboard keys.
- Component is an older name for integration. Component also has a separate meaning in this design system.
- Home Assistant Supervised is a deprecated installation method. Home Assistant Core is still the main program.

Use the current name when you give an instruction. Keep an old key when you explain saved configuration. Check the [official installation guide](https://www.home-assistant.io/installation/) before you recommend an installation method.

## What this page does not cover

It covers the 83 glossary entries, not the whole Home Assistant website. The [terminology JSON](../reference/ha-terminology.json) has the sources, aliases, IDs and dates. [Interface terminology](interface-terminology.html) covers screens and settings. A term that is not here needs its own source.
